{
 "voice": "archive (bm_fable 0.40 + am_michael 0.40 + bm_lewis 0.20)",
 "style_md5": "c9ce4988",
 "speed": 0.92,
 "question_speed": 0.8522,
 "duration": 834.92,
 "chunks": [
  {
   "text": "On the first of July, nineteen forty-six, the United States dropped an atomic bomb on one of its own battleships.",
   "start": 0.35,
   "end": 7.487,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 0,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "0dac33a04c3b.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Three weeks later, it set off a second one.",
   "start": 7.787,
   "end": 10.183,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 0,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "3b51866bcd93.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She survived them both.",
   "start": 10.483,
   "end": 12.037,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 0,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "8cba6055357a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Navy had painted her bright orange, so the bomber could not miss.",
   "start": 12.637,
   "end": 16.769,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 1,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b638c985ef49.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The first bomb missed her by about a third of a mile.",
   "start": 17.069,
   "end": 19.976,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 1,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "834fba384d28.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "When the smoke cleared, she was still floating.",
   "start": 20.276,
   "end": 22.608,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 1,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "3b95d0cce54b.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The second bomb went off under the water, about a thousand yards away.",
   "start": 23.208,
   "end": 27.263,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 2,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "24c062ed44b0.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "It sank a battleship and an aircraft carrier nearby.",
   "start": 27.563,
   "end": 30.588,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 2,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "ce7d4a4b8637.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She was still floating.",
   "start": 30.888,
   "end": 32.209,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 2,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d1923a32d155.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "This is the USS Nevada.",
   "start": 32.809,
   "end": 34.937,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 3,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "39672d51bcfc.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "It was not the first time she refused to die.",
   "start": 35.537,
   "end": 38.209,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 4,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "eaa03e8d9b26.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Five years earlier, at Pearl Harbor, she was the only battleship that got under way.",
   "start": 38.509,
   "end": 43.439,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 4,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "94689cf799cd.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "So if two atomic bombs could not sink her, what did?",
   "start": 44.039,
   "end": 47.602,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 5,
   "speed": 0.8522,
   "file": "95994b8a28ee.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "And where is she now?",
   "start": 47.902,
   "end": 49.202,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 5,
   "speed": 0.8522,
   "file": "76d2c589bec4.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "For more than seventy years, nobody could say.",
   "start": 49.502,
   "end": 52.166,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 5,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "dd7315c268e8.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Start with the place.",
   "start": 53.066,
   "end": 54.35,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 6,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d3c48cdf0b78.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Bikini Atoll, in the Marshall Islands, in the middle of the Pacific.",
   "start": 54.65,
   "end": 58.654,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 6,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "29cfea9d3807.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "A ring of small islands around a lagoon about twenty miles long.",
   "start": 58.954,
   "end": 62.979,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 6,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "23fd18dc4a42.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Its people, one hundred and sixty-two of them, had already been moved off the atoll in March.",
   "start": 63.579,
   "end": 69.043,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 7,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "ce9fc143f421.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In the summer of nineteen forty-six, the lagoon held a fleet.",
   "start": 69.343,
   "end": 73.045,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 7,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b6a85bcfd552.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "About ninety target ships, anchored on purpose where an atomic bomb would fall.",
   "start": 73.345,
   "end": 78.005,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 7,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "a1c43be272f2.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The operation was called Crossroads.",
   "start": 78.605,
   "end": 80.86,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 8,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b35a1ae4dae6.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Its question was simple.",
   "start": 81.16,
   "end": 82.773,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 8,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "3ae568d12c5c.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "What does an atomic bomb do to a navy?",
   "start": 83.073,
   "end": 85.542,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 8,
   "speed": 0.8522,
   "file": "019bb6a0e8f7.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "About forty-two thousand men took part, with two hundred and forty-two ships and one hundred and fifty-six aircraft.",
   "start": 86.142,
   "end": 93.326,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 9,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "03426abccefa.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Cameras were set up on towers, on islands, and in planes.",
   "start": 93.626,
   "end": 97.289,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 9,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "ce3c3d359d07.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The targets were old American warships, captured German and Japanese ships, and small craft.",
   "start": 97.889,
   "end": 103.789,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 10,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "7fae3d20fc5d.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Many carried animals.",
   "start": 104.089,
   "end": 105.656,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 10,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f84c34b6b807.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Goats, pigs and rats were placed on board to see what the blast would do to a living crew.",
   "start": 105.956,
   "end": 111.237,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 10,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "8ebf0f15a154.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "At the centre of it all was one ship.",
   "start": 111.837,
   "end": 113.998,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 11,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "8b915f192a21.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Navy chose her as the bull's-eye.",
   "start": 114.298,
   "end": 116.568,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 11,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "2cffe68d081f.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The point the bomber would aim at.",
   "start": 116.868,
   "end": 118.817,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 11,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "480b87814c4e.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "They painted her international orange, with white trim, so she would stand out from every other ship in the lagoon.",
   "start": 119.417,
   "end": 125.846,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 12,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "17269547825c.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "A flashing light on board marked her for the bombardier.",
   "start": 126.146,
   "end": 129.358,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 12,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "5dc305a82494.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the twenty-eighth of May, she had sailed into the lagoon with a crew of four hundred and three.",
   "start": 129.958,
   "end": 134.982,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 13,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "55ee592d12bc.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the thirtieth of June, the crew left her.",
   "start": 135.282,
   "end": 137.725,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 13,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "4f411c7bf616.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Behind them, in her pilot house, they left goats and rats.",
   "start": 138.025,
   "end": 141.503,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 13,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "a5907c8dae99.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Why this ship?",
   "start": 142.103,
   "end": 143.168,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 14,
   "speed": 0.8522,
   "file": "aa9951dc4c49.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Why make the Nevada the target?",
   "start": 143.468,
   "end": 145.639,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 14,
   "speed": 0.8522,
   "file": "8164844e93cc.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "To understand what the Navy was aiming at, go back to a Sunday morning in Hawaii.",
   "start": 145.939,
   "end": 150.839,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 14,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "056ff441a6cc.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Pearl Harbor.",
   "start": 151.739,
   "end": 152.658,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 15,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "a1354f5d14cf.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The seventh of December, nineteen forty-one.",
   "start": 152.958,
   "end": 155.631,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 15,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "67e07b6f7383.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Along the east side of Ford Island lay the Pacific Fleet's battleships, most of them moored in pairs.",
   "start": 155.931,
   "end": 162.158,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 15,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "504120f74f37.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Nevada lay alone, at the end of the line, just astern of the USS Arizona.",
   "start": 162.758,
   "end": 168.015,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 16,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d698e871e8d8.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "At about one minute past eight, Japanese planes came over the harbour.",
   "start": 168.615,
   "end": 172.897,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 17,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "75ecd502f936.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Within minutes, a torpedo tore into the Nevada's port bow.",
   "start": 173.197,
   "end": 176.673,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 17,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "8cc0ce073c25.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "It was a Sunday, and many officers were ashore.",
   "start": 177.273,
   "end": 180.007,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 18,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f5d0365d9e76.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The senior officer on board was a reserve lieutenant commander named Francis Thomas.",
   "start": 180.307,
   "end": 185.485,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 18,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "95d4616ce82e.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the Arizona blew up.",
   "start": 186.085,
   "end": 187.78,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 19,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "ff00e0bcb3c5.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Burning oil spread across the water and drifted toward the Nevada.",
   "start": 188.08,
   "end": 191.954,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 19,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "5bdb3d24212f.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Staying meant burning with the Arizona.",
   "start": 192.554,
   "end": 194.863,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 20,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "aba31c9864be.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "So the crew did something no other battleship managed that morning.",
   "start": 195.163,
   "end": 198.89,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 20,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "19580ade0a33.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "They got her moving.",
   "start": 199.19,
   "end": 200.459,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 20,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "936371624ac4.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "A battleship normally left her berth with the help of tugs.",
   "start": 201.059,
   "end": 204.459,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 21,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "c4550c3fbbf6.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "There were no tugs.",
   "start": 204.759,
   "end": 205.995,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 21,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "af1eb81f48f5.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "But her chief quartermaster, Sedberry, had already told the engine room to get ready, before any officer reached the bridge.",
   "start": 206.295,
   "end": 213.352,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 21,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "9b2b0daffbc3.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Chief Boatswain Edwin Hill led a party onto the quay under fire.",
   "start": 213.952,
   "end": 217.93,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 22,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "dbadadf3eedf.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "They cast off her lines.",
   "start": 218.23,
   "end": 219.827,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 22,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "fba25f16d178.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Then Hill swam back out to the ship.",
   "start": 220.127,
   "end": 222.284,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 22,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "c10b54663135.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "At about twenty to nine, without tugs, the Nevada backed away from her berth and headed down the channel toward the open sea.",
   "start": 222.884,
   "end": 230.256,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 23,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "6f2e7f1c187c.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "A single battleship, on fire, moving past the wreckage of the fleet.",
   "start": 230.856,
   "end": 235.008,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 24,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "3e91243bee74.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Japanese saw her too.",
   "start": 235.608,
   "end": 237.26,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 25,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "e970df64e4c7.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In the second wave, dive bombers went for her.",
   "start": 237.56,
   "end": 240.114,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 25,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "e00aa7e5f27a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She was hit by at least six bombs.",
   "start": 240.714,
   "end": 242.693,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 26,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "0e7592c4ae66.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Her forward decks were on fire.",
   "start": 242.993,
   "end": 244.894,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 26,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "513f0f74c51e.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Water was pouring in.",
   "start": 245.194,
   "end": 246.594,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 26,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "eabfe2c2215c.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the boat deck, a young ensign named Taussig was badly wounded.",
   "start": 247.194,
   "end": 251.278,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 27,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "a67b6f31cfb4.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "He refused to leave his anti-aircraft guns.",
   "start": 251.578,
   "end": 254.403,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 27,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "49e0fabb25b5.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In the end, his men had to lower him down on a stretcher.",
   "start": 254.703,
   "end": 257.952,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 27,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "64a024fee6b8.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Now there was a new danger.",
   "start": 258.552,
   "end": 260.251,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 28,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "598e18845873.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "If she sank in the narrow channel, she could block it, and trap the whole fleet inside Pearl Harbor.",
   "start": 260.551,
   "end": 266.308,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 28,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "112d509bdbc0.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She was ordered out of the channel.",
   "start": 266.908,
   "end": 268.685,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 29,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "db663ad74416.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "At about ten past nine, she ran aground near Hospital Point.",
   "start": 268.985,
   "end": 273.074,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 29,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "ea169f986c4b.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the forecastle, Chief Boatswain Hill was trying to let go the anchors when bombs exploded around him.",
   "start": 273.674,
   "end": 279.591,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 30,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "29e35699f0c5.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "He was killed.",
   "start": 279.891,
   "end": 280.884,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 30,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "5d17355614a1.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "He was awarded the Medal of Honor.",
   "start": 281.184,
   "end": 283.187,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 30,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "dff5bca0e4ea.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Below decks, Machinist Donald Ross stayed in a dynamo room full of smoke and steam until he was blinded and knocked unconscious.",
   "start": 283.787,
   "end": 292.035,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 31,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f21c81b503e5.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "When he came round, he went back to work.",
   "start": 292.335,
   "end": 294.565,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 31,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "052932fd22d7.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "He collapsed a second time.",
   "start": 294.865,
   "end": 296.604,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 31,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "edceba40f258.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "He also received the Medal of Honor.",
   "start": 296.904,
   "end": 299.218,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 31,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "af4e9c6d5f4e.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Later that morning, tugs pulled her free and pushed her across the channel.",
   "start": 299.818,
   "end": 303.827,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 32,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "7cefd352b1fa.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "At a quarter to eleven, she was grounded a second time, stern first, at Waipio Point.",
   "start": 304.127,
   "end": 309.56,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 32,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f276ebac9cd3.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The channel stayed open.",
   "start": 309.86,
   "end": 311.341,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 32,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "eacec5bd34d3.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She had a crew of nearly fifteen hundred.",
   "start": 311.941,
   "end": 314.19,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 33,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "2114a2fc6713.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Close to sixty of them were killed.",
   "start": 314.49,
   "end": 316.577,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 33,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f269099d91f6.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "More than a hundred were wounded.",
   "start": 316.877,
   "end": 318.635,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 33,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "5b53581d3926.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "But the Nevada had done what no other battleship did that day.",
   "start": 318.935,
   "end": 322.511,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 33,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "a63ee7da6179.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She had fought back, and she had moved.",
   "start": 322.811,
   "end": 324.844,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 33,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "5f390407908a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "By the next day, she had settled onto the bottom in shallow water.",
   "start": 325.744,
   "end": 329.371,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 34,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "e5761cf06a3f.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "For most ships, that would have been the end of the story.",
   "start": 329.671,
   "end": 332.549,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 34,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "183b1698e778.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Divers made more than four hundred dives, and spent more than fifteen hundred hours inside her flooded hull.",
   "start": 333.149,
   "end": 339.465,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 35,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b6765f5f9cef.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Two salvage men died from poison gas that had built up in her compartments.",
   "start": 339.765,
   "end": 344.566,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 35,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "87ee15667455.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the twelfth of February, nineteen forty-two, the Nevada floated again.",
   "start": 345.166,
   "end": 349.544,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 36,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "a82df25e6b96.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In April she sailed for Puget Sound, on the West Coast, to be rebuilt.",
   "start": 349.844,
   "end": 354.419,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 36,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d4ff8d95a3ef.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She came back to the war in nineteen forty-three, off the frozen island of Attu, in the Aleutians.",
   "start": 355.019,
   "end": 361.125,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 37,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "dcbfc3588c1a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Then she crossed to the Atlantic.",
   "start": 361.725,
   "end": 363.704,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 38,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "796eb184a353.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the sixth of June, nineteen forty-four, she was off Utah Beach in Normandy, firing on German positions ahead of the landings.",
   "start": 364.004,
   "end": 372.087,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 38,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "8a329caf1a10.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Of all the battleships at Pearl Harbor that morning, the Nevada was the only one at D-Day.",
   "start": 372.687,
   "end": 377.972,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 39,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "97033e95f1c5.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "That day alone, she fired hundreds of her big fourteen-inch shells.",
   "start": 378.572,
   "end": 382.365,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 40,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f70c0df5f55a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the twenty-fifth of June, she shelled the fortress port of Cherbourg.",
   "start": 382.965,
   "end": 386.813,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 41,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "96874cc6456f.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "German batteries fired back and straddled her more than twenty times.",
   "start": 387.113,
   "end": 391.322,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 41,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "210d11a1e359.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She was not hit.",
   "start": 391.622,
   "end": 392.789,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 41,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "a156c0663536.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In August, she moved to the Mediterranean and duelled the heavy guns at Toulon, in southern France.",
   "start": 393.089,
   "end": 399.315,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 41,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b80897488b59.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Then she went back to the Pacific.",
   "start": 399.915,
   "end": 401.657,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 42,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "c7dc9850398e.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In February nineteen forty-five, she was off Iwo Jima.",
   "start": 401.957,
   "end": 405.705,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 42,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "7af1b75bc06c.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In March, off Okinawa, a kamikaze crashed into her deck near her number three turret.",
   "start": 406.305,
   "end": 411.795,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 43,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "20e394f2909a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Eleven men were killed.",
   "start": 412.095,
   "end": 413.613,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 43,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "3f77757001ca.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Days later, a shore battery hit her.",
   "start": 414.213,
   "end": 416.392,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 44,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d0accc0d1ba0.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Two more were killed.",
   "start": 416.692,
   "end": 417.938,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 44,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "32c36c718d0d.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She kept firing.",
   "start": 418.238,
   "end": 419.42,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 44,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "1a1e3ed9e605.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She finished the war with seven battle stars.",
   "start": 420.02,
   "end": 422.534,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 45,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "68c5a588d5aa.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She was also one of the oldest battleships the Navy still had.",
   "start": 422.834,
   "end": 426.324,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 45,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "05384b4b03c7.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Launched in nineteen fourteen.",
   "start": 426.624,
   "end": 428.543,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 45,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "254e7c7dde07.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Built for a different kind of war.",
   "start": 428.843,
   "end": 430.645,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 45,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "9199bd9f60ae.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "When the war ended, the Navy had more battleships than it needed.",
   "start": 431.245,
   "end": 434.766,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 46,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d0b674765e81.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Old ones were going to the scrapyard.",
   "start": 435.066,
   "end": 437.239,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 46,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "6be65329e600.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Nevada had survived a torpedo, bombs, a beaching, a kamikaze and shore batteries on two oceans.",
   "start": 437.839,
   "end": 444.792,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 47,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "50e2b086c0d3.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "That made her exactly what the Crossroads planners wanted.",
   "start": 445.092,
   "end": 448.545,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 47,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "aeb44b8a8ab8.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "A tough old ship to test the most powerful weapon ever made.",
   "start": 448.845,
   "end": 452.555,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 47,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "bb0ce7b4c857.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The first of July, nineteen forty-six.",
   "start": 453.455,
   "end": 456.187,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 48,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "080a4c25ed9a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Test Able.",
   "start": 456.487,
   "end": 457.477,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 48,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "faee12de701f.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "From Kwajalein, a few hours' flight away, a B-29 bomber named Dave's Dream took off with the bomb.",
   "start": 458.077,
   "end": 464.502,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 49,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "807810f3a5d6.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Nevada's own crew watched from a transport about twenty-one miles away.",
   "start": 465.102,
   "end": 469.588,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 50,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "9c9c4a628cb5.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "At thirty-four seconds past nine in the morning, the bomb went off, about five hundred and twenty feet above the lagoon.",
   "start": 470.188,
   "end": 477.245,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 51,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "eebe498d08c5.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Its force was about twenty thousand tons of TNT.",
   "start": 477.845,
   "end": 481.407,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 52,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "962e89efaee6.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "It was the same type of bomb that destroyed Nagasaki less than a year earlier.",
   "start": 481.707,
   "end": 486.312,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 52,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "e1b9ae39f0df.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "But the bomb did not explode over the Nevada.",
   "start": 486.912,
   "end": 489.568,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 53,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "3a8c77b0e1b7.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "It went off about a third of a mile away.",
   "start": 489.868,
   "end": 492.297,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 53,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "eb897eb11d53.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Almost on top of the transport Gilliam.",
   "start": 492.597,
   "end": 495.078,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 53,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "3e0587f124bc.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Nobody ever found out exactly why it missed.",
   "start": 495.678,
   "end": 498.621,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 54,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "06e93f53d84c.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Five ships sank.",
   "start": 499.221,
   "end": 500.491,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 55,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "5b903a1b7b47.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Gilliam and the transport Carlisle went down first.",
   "start": 500.791,
   "end": 503.877,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 55,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "aa5258022cf0.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the destroyers Lamson and Anderson.",
   "start": 504.177,
   "end": 506.667,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 55,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "244ef17e9de6.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The next day, the Japanese cruiser Sakawa followed them.",
   "start": 506.967,
   "end": 510.48,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 55,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "8fc11a5e1c48.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Nevada was hit by the blast and the heat.",
   "start": 511.08,
   "end": 513.678,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 56,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "537a926be656.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Both of her topmasts came down.",
   "start": 513.978,
   "end": 515.981,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 56,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "9f4ed36f49bd.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Her superstructure was dished in.",
   "start": 516.281,
   "end": 518.339,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 56,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "ea020915cd8b.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Fires broke out on her decks.",
   "start": 518.639,
   "end": 520.569,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 56,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "ce67cb7c1463.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Her boilers were put out of action.",
   "start": 520.869,
   "end": 522.822,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 56,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "664e6cb3af88.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "One of her floatplanes was torn loose and thrown upside down onto the deck.",
   "start": 523.122,
   "end": 527.355,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 56,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "67177f5315f4.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "But her hull was almost untouched.",
   "start": 527.955,
   "end": 530.065,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 57,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "4b85ac3036b4.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "And in her pilot house, the Navy's inspectors found the goats and rats.",
   "start": 530.365,
   "end": 534.644,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 57,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "ba30645bd052.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The report says they were apparently unaffected by the heat and the blast.",
   "start": 534.944,
   "end": 539.098,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 57,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "13907ebc8119.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The orange ship had taken an atomic bomb, and she was still floating.",
   "start": 539.698,
   "end": 543.728,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 58,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "c4d8021fbc8b.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The first test had sunk five ships out of about ninety.",
   "start": 544.628,
   "end": 547.928,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 59,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "fd913b6a7f99.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The bomb had not wiped out the fleet.",
   "start": 548.228,
   "end": 550.333,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 59,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "8c785f3578aa.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The second test would be very different.",
   "start": 550.633,
   "end": 552.964,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 59,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "7c8ddef59dce.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The twenty-fifth of July, nineteen forty-six.",
   "start": 553.564,
   "end": 556.631,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 60,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f8de3890cf8e.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Test Baker.",
   "start": 556.931,
   "end": 557.974,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 60,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "6a26b51a3203.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "This time the bomb was not dropped.",
   "start": 558.574,
   "end": 560.666,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 61,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "841f76135c86.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "It hung under a landing ship, ninety feet beneath the surface of the lagoon.",
   "start": 560.966,
   "end": 565.381,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 61,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "c4038be71782.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "At about eight thirty-five in the morning, it went off.",
   "start": 565.981,
   "end": 569.017,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 62,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "7592bc778270.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Another bomb of about twenty kilotons.",
   "start": 569.317,
   "end": 571.635,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 62,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "6720d9a7fa03.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "A column of water rose about a mile into the air.",
   "start": 572.235,
   "end": 575.396,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 63,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "713e56216e80.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Millions of tons of seawater lifted out of the lagoon, then fell back onto the fleet.",
   "start": 575.696,
   "end": 580.648,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 63,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "70f30c4bc486.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The old battleship Arkansas was about two hundred and forty yards away.",
   "start": 581.248,
   "end": 585.698,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 64,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "7726cb2d2001.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She went down.",
   "start": 585.998,
   "end": 587.066,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 64,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "2df6baf1aed5.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The aircraft carrier Saratoga, about three hundred and eighty yards away, sank that afternoon.",
   "start": 587.366,
   "end": 593.066,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 64,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "e1360e1de7a7.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Four days later, the Japanese battleship Nagato sank too.",
   "start": 593.366,
   "end": 597.139,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 64,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b39b7791c127.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Nevada was about a thousand and sixty yards from the bomb.",
   "start": 597.739,
   "end": 601.371,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 65,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f90f7fddd3dd.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Her crew watched from sixteen miles away.",
   "start": 601.671,
   "end": 604.101,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 65,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "1b7e08566176.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The shock hit her hull.",
   "start": 604.401,
   "end": 605.889,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 65,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "79ae78805452.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Some compartments aft flooded.",
   "start": 606.189,
   "end": 608.08,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 65,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "a2d4da31685e.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She took a slight list.",
   "start": 608.38,
   "end": 609.727,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 65,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "4a22f8994e7e.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "And she was still floating.",
   "start": 610.327,
   "end": 611.753,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 66,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "21e757a60da7.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She was not the only one.",
   "start": 612.353,
   "end": 613.853,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 67,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "ec50edbbb37c.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The old battleships New York and Pennsylvania also came through both tests.",
   "start": 614.153,
   "end": 618.883,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 67,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "65b1e9c9c360.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "But the Nevada was the one they had aimed the first bomb at.",
   "start": 619.183,
   "end": 622.444,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 67,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "9f5a1a91c191.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "And she had now taken both.",
   "start": 622.744,
   "end": 624.432,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 67,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "a58538c5b07d.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "But this time, surviving was the problem.",
   "start": 625.032,
   "end": 627.511,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 68,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "088aef1745d0.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The water that fell on the fleet carried the bomb's radiation.",
   "start": 627.811,
   "end": 631.416,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 68,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "ecc0131ea8c9.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Navy's inspectors called the Nevada highly radioactive, inside and outside.",
   "start": 632.016,
   "end": 637.348,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 69,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "4596d7d43751.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sailors tried to wash the target ships down with hoses, chemicals and lye.",
   "start": 637.948,
   "end": 642.592,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 70,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d7323a8d8ebe.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "It did not work.",
   "start": 642.892,
   "end": 644.079,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 70,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "78d04a3541c9.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The contamination stayed for weeks.",
   "start": 644.379,
   "end": 646.409,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 70,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "7c8097e44064.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Nevada had survived two atomic bombs.",
   "start": 647.009,
   "end": 649.763,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 71,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "aa5783b50353.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Now nobody could live on her.",
   "start": 650.063,
   "end": 652.021,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 71,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b9ea3efe4008.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the twenty-ninth of August, nineteen forty-six, at Kwajalein, the Nevada was decommissioned.",
   "start": 652.921,
   "end": 658.752,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 72,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f424e78b8b03.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The ship that refused to sink was still afloat.",
   "start": 659.052,
   "end": 661.91,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 72,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "856da6a04b90.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "But her life as a warship was over.",
   "start": 662.21,
   "end": 664.503,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 72,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "5188ba7193a5.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Navy studied her for almost two more years.",
   "start": 665.103,
   "end": 667.72,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 73,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "4a69b2366393.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In May nineteen forty-seven, she was towed to Pearl Harbor, the same harbour she had escaped from, for radiological tests.",
   "start": 668.02,
   "end": 675.804,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 73,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "92856f6776c7.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the Navy decided how she would end.",
   "start": 676.404,
   "end": 679.029,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 74,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "42d635fa9671.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She would be one last target.",
   "start": 679.328,
   "end": 681.07,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 74,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "ae3b16ed83d6.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the twenty-sixth of July, nineteen forty-eight, a tug towed her out to sea, southwest of Oahu.",
   "start": 681.67,
   "end": 687.888,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 75,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "527c466e257c.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "First, new secret explosives were tested on her.",
   "start": 688.488,
   "end": 691.582,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 76,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "805fb186cbdd.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "They ripped holes in her sides.",
   "start": 691.882,
   "end": 693.63,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 76,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "c0e0793afd08.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She did not sink.",
   "start": 693.93,
   "end": 695.143,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 76,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "7a5074dff2a5.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Days of bombs and rockets followed.",
   "start": 695.743,
   "end": 698.017,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 77,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b66cff82625d.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She was still floating.",
   "start": 698.317,
   "end": 699.638,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 77,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d1923a32d155.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "On her last day, the cruisers Astoria and Pasadena opened fire.",
   "start": 700.238,
   "end": 704.573,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 78,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "835dd22bd4fd.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the battleship Iowa joined them.",
   "start": 704.873,
   "end": 706.95,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 78,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "76bbfe7d043e.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In about twenty minutes, the three ships fired two hundred and eighty-seven shells at her.",
   "start": 707.55,
   "end": 712.524,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 79,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "6ee05fbd2eef.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Twenty-seven of them came from the Iowa's sixteen-inch guns.",
   "start": 712.824,
   "end": 716.275,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 79,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "13de59fa6592.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Nevada was burning.",
   "start": 716.875,
   "end": 718.466,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 80,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f65653790133.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She was still floating.",
   "start": 718.766,
   "end": 720.087,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 80,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d1923a32d155.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In the end, it took torpedo bombers.",
   "start": 720.687,
   "end": 723.093,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 81,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "6164b44acf00.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Several torpedoes hit her.",
   "start": 723.393,
   "end": 725.086,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 81,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "9654f8d86f3d.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Then one smashed into her side, amidships.",
   "start": 725.386,
   "end": 728.081,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 81,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "46e7ad43a65b.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She rolled over, and sank.",
   "start": 728.681,
   "end": 730.386,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 82,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b4c3cc128d98.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The admiral who watched her go said, \"She was a grand old ship.\"",
   "start": 730.986,
   "end": 734.663,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 83,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "772bb557d68c.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She had survived Pearl Harbor.",
   "start": 735.263,
   "end": 737.056,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 84,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "73bbb408a7d6.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Two oceans of war.",
   "start": 737.356,
   "end": 738.76,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 84,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "680cfa451e46.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Two atomic bombs.",
   "start": 739.06,
   "end": 740.471,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 84,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f2a226dbaca9.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In the end, it took four days, three warships and the aircraft of her own navy to sink her.",
   "start": 740.771,
   "end": 746.161,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 84,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "4f42b2d8d022.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "According to the archaeologists who later studied her, she took something else down with her.",
   "start": 746.761,
   "end": 751.637,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 85,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b5b2270aa444.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Three fourteen-inch guns that had once belonged to the USS Arizona, her neighbour on Battleship Row.",
   "start": 751.937,
   "end": 758.382,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 85,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b51521843fa8.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "So that is what sank her.",
   "start": 758.982,
   "end": 760.56,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 86,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "c3c404518e53.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Her own navy.",
   "start": 760.86,
   "end": 761.946,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 86,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "e8826c2913c1.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "But for more than seventy years, nobody knew exactly where she lay.",
   "start": 762.846,
   "end": 766.623,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 87,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "4f9620e0424f.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The logs from nineteen forty-eight gave only rough positions.",
   "start": 766.923,
   "end": 770.857,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 87,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d1061efb2d39.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "And the water there is nearly three miles deep.",
   "start": 771.157,
   "end": 773.969,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 87,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "6a21943deaf8.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In twenty sixteen, a researcher with NOAA went back to those logs, the logs of the Iowa, the Astoria and the Pasadena, and worked out where she had gone down.",
   "start": 774.569,
   "end": 784.217,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 88,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "589c62676454.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In April twenty twenty, the survey ship Pacific Constructor searched that area with an underwater robot.",
   "start": 784.817,
   "end": 791.413,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 89,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f016b97f3eb8.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "It was run by two private companies, Ocean Infinity and SEARCH.",
   "start": 791.713,
   "end": 795.841,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 89,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "996a86559a6a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In May, they announced it.",
   "start": 796.441,
   "end": 798.054,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 90,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "0e5a5ea04451.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "They had found the Nevada.",
   "start": 798.354,
   "end": 799.798,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 90,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "c9d2b1b97ee2.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She lies about sixty-five nautical miles southwest of Pearl Harbor, more than fifteen thousand four hundred feet down.",
   "start": 800.398,
   "end": 807.501,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 91,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "e5d6df8dfbc9.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She is upside down.",
   "start": 808.101,
   "end": 809.565,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 92,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "02e7bc637c82.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Her bow and her stern have broken away.",
   "start": 809.865,
   "end": 812.282,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 92,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "fb69d6ebc28b.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "On her stern, the number thirty-six can still be read.",
   "start": 812.582,
   "end": 815.784,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 92,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "9ced166cc225.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She is still the property of the United States Navy, protected by federal law.",
   "start": 816.384,
   "end": 820.989,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 93,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "16ef07642745.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Many people say she should have been saved as a museum ship.",
   "start": 821.589,
   "end": 824.871,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 94,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "5d9accf49a4a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Instead, her own navy used her as a target until she sank.",
   "start": 825.171,
   "end": 829.196,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 94,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "822d2d05c5ad.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "What do you think?",
   "start": 829.796,
   "end": 830.976,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 95,
   "speed": 0.8522,
   "file": "51fc1731f950.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Was that the right way to end the Nevada's story?",
   "start": 831.276,
   "end": 833.92,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 95,
   "speed": 0.8522,
   "file": "1f7ec7f59a23.wav"
  }
 ]
}